  birdingRating: 4.5,
  date: 'February 20, 2024',
  excerpt: 'Supporting meaningful conservation while having incredible wildlife experiences.',
  fullReview: 'As someone passionate about conservation, this tour aligned perfectly with my values. Ol Pejeta\'s rhino sanctuary is doing vital work - seeing both black and white rhinos thriving was inspiring. The chimpanzee refuge provides excellent care for rescued chimps. Samburu showed community-based conservation working beautifully. Guides explained conservation challenges and successes throughout. Wildlife viewing was exceptional - all Big Five plus rare species. Luxury accommodations were eco-friendly without compromising comfort. Knowing my money supports conservation made the experience even more meaningful. Kenya is leading Africa in conservation tourism. Highly recommend for conscious travelers!',
