  excerpt: 'Challenging trek rewarded with spectacular summit sunrise and beautiful landscapes.',
  fullReview: 'Mount Kenya trek was everything I hoped for! The Sirimon route takes you through stunning montane forest into otherworldly moorlands with giant groundsels and lobelias. Point Lenana summit at 4,985m at sunrise was absolutely breathtaking - watching the sun rise over Africa from that height was emotional and unforgettable. The descent via Chogoria offered different scenery with beautiful lakes and waterfalls. Our guides and porters were professional and supportive throughout. Altitude was challenging but manageable with proper acclimatization. Budget-friendly compared to Kilimanjaro but equally spectacular. Mount Kenya deserves more recognition. Highly recommend for trekkers!',
