  birdingRating: 4.2,
  date: 'December 19, 2021',
  excerpt: 'Unique accommodation experience with good wildlife viewing.',
  fullReview: 'The Tsavo and Taita safari featuring Salt Lick Lodge was memorable. Salt Lick is architectural marvel - elevated lodge with animals coming to waterhole below. Watched elephants, buffalo, and countless other animals from room balcony at night. Tsavo East game drives were productive with good elephant and cat sightings. The red soil gives unique photos. Guide was experienced and professional. Taita Hills sanctuary was smaller but still enjoyable. Food at both lodges was excellent. Only downside was long drives between locations. Three days felt a bit rushed. Would have preferred four days to enjoy Salt Lick more. Still highly recommend for unique lodge experience combined with solid wildlife viewing.',
