  excerpt: 'Solid experience but manage your expectations for budget tour.',
  fullReview: 'The 3-day Masai Mara budget safari was acceptable for the price but had limitations. Wildlife viewing was reasonable - saw lions, elephants, giraffes, and lots of herbivores. Missed seeing leopards and cheetahs which was disappointing. Budget accommodation meant cold showers and basic facilities but we knew this booking. Food was repetitive - same breakfast every day. Vehicle was crowded with seven people making photography challenging. Our guide was okay though not particularly engaging or knowledgeable. The Mara itself is beautiful and has abundant wildlife. For $999 it\'s fair value but don\'t expect luxury or premium experience. Better suited for young travelers or those on tight budget. If you can afford it, recommend paying more for better accommodation and smaller group size.',
