  bushVibe: 3.8,
  sceneryRating: 4.0,
  birdingRating: 3.7,
  date: 'July 18, 2019',
  excerpt: 'Saw great wildlife but felt hurried throughout.',
  fullReview: 'The 4-day Mara and Nakuru tour covered good ground but pacing felt rushed. Masai Mara game drives were productive with lion and elephant sightings. Lake Nakuru delivered flamingos and rhinos as promised. However, spent significant time driving between locations when could have been viewing wildlife. Check-out times meant missing best morning light at Lake Nakuru. Accommodations were comfortable mid-range. Food was good with some excellent meals. Our guide was knowledgeable but seemed focused on sticking to schedule rather than maximizing wildlife opportunities. Would have preferred three full days in Mara and skip Nakuru, or add extra day. The parks themselves are wonderful but tour structure could be improved. Still decent value overall despite rushed feeling.',
