  sceneryRating: 3.7,
  birdingRating: 3.2,
  date: 'May 9, 2019',
  excerpt: 'Some good moments but several disappointments too.',
  fullReview: 'Our Tsavo and Amboseli safari had ups and downs. Amboseli elephants were magnificent and we got lucky with Kilimanjaro views one morning. Tsavo felt very empty during our visit - guide explained animals dispersed due to recent rains providing water everywhere. Saw some wildlife but nothing spectacular. The long beach extension was nice break though hotel was undergoing renovations causing noise. Food throughout was average. Our vehicle had AC issues during hottest days which was uncomfortable. Guide was friendly but not particularly informative. For the price expected better overall experience. Kenya\'s parks have great potential but timing and luck play big role. Would consider returning during dry season when wildlife concentrations are higher.',
