  date: 'January 18, 2019',
  excerpt: 'Good budget option with decent wildlife viewing.',
  fullReview: 'The shared 6-day circuit safari offered good value for money. Group of six passengers made it affordable while still allowing everyone window seats. Wildlife viewing was productive across all three parks - saw four of Big Five (missed leopard) plus abundant plains game. Masai Mara was highlight with massive herds and lions. Lake Nakuru delivered rhinos and birds. Amboseli elephants were magnificent. Accommodations were mid-range budget - clean and comfortable enough. Food was decent with some excellent meals. Guide was knowledgeable though sometimes rushed. Vehicle was older but functional. Long drives between parks were tiring. Fellow travelers were friendly making the shared experience enjoyable. For those on budget wanting to see Kenya\'s highlights, this works well. Just don\'t expect luxury.',
