  migration: {
    title: 'Wildebeest Migration',
    description: 'Kenya’s wildebeest migration is a breathtaking natural wonder, as more than two million wildebeest, zebra, and gazelle pour into the Masai Mara each year. From July to October, the plains come alive with thundering herds, dramatic river crossings, and unforgettable predator action, offering travelers a rare chance to witness Africa’s raw beauty and incredible wildlife on a truly epic scale.'
  },

  highlights: {
    title: 'Wildlife Highlights',
    description: 'Kenya is full of jaw-dropping wildlife moments that stay with you forever. Picture lions hunting at dawn in the Masai Mara, elephants marching beneath Mount Kilimanjaro in Amboseli, and the heart-stopping rush of wildebeest leaping into the Mara River. Spotting a leopard draped on an acacia branch, rhinos grazing in Ol Pejeta, or flamingos painting Lake Nakuru pink are the kind of magical “aha!” sightings that make Kenya one of the world’s most thrilling safari destinations.'
  },

  bestTime: {
    title: 'Best Time for Wildlife Viewing',
    description: 'Kenya delivers exceptional wildlife experiences year-round, but June to October stands out as the prime safari window. During this Dry season, the Masai Mara hosts the world-famous wildebeest migration, with massive herds arriving from July or August until October before returning to Tanzania. These peak months draw many visitors, while November to April offers superb birdwatching with vibrant migratory species.'
  },

