  excerpt: 'No crowds, patient guide, perfect light. Got portfolio-worthy wildlife shots!',
  fullReview: 'Specifically chose Ruaha for serious wildlife photography and it delivered beyond expectations! The remoteness meant exclusive sightings with no vehicles crowding shots or disturbing animals. Guide understood photography needs perfectly - positioning for golden hour light, patience for behavioral moments, and deep knowledge of animal patterns. Photographed wild dogs mid-hunt, lions with fresh kills in perfect light, and leopards against stunning backdrops. Walking safari along Great Ruaha River offered unique ground-level perspectives rarely possible. Landscapes were diverse - ancient baobabs, rocky kopjes, and dramatic river scenes. Accommodations had good lighting for editing. Hidden gem for serious wildlife photographers!',
