  fullReview: 'What made this safari unique was authentic cultural component. Maasai village visit was not touristy show but genuine interaction - learned about traditions, daily life, even tried some traditional food. Warriors showed us fire-making technique and explained medicinal plants. Boat safari in Nyerere was peaceful and saw hippos, crocodiles, and diverse birdlife up close. Mikumi game drives produced good wildlife sightings including wild dogs which guide said was lucky. Accommodations were simple but clean. Group size was small which was nice. Really appreciated this wasn\'t just another standard safari but included meaningful cultural exchange.',
