  excerpt: 'Ruaha felt wild and remote. Fewer tourists made it more authentic.',
  fullReview: 'Deliberately chose this tour to avoid crowded northern circuit and so glad we did! Ruaha was spectacularly remote and wild - drove hours without seeing another vehicle. Wildlife was different too - saw wild dogs (very rare!), greater kudu, roan antelope not found up north. Lion prides were massive. Elephants everywhere. SGR train ride from Dar was comfortable and scenic. Mikumi was good warm-up with easy sightings. Accommodations were simple but authentic bush camps with excellent food. Guide was passionate about Ruaha and knew it intimately. Only downside was long distances. For adventurous travelers wanting authentic uncrowded experience, this perfect alternative to busier parks.',
