  date: 'May 3, 2024',
  excerpt: 'Eight days perfect length. Cultural experiences added depth to safari.',
  fullReview: 'Eight days allowed for really comprehensive experience without feeling rushed. Kilimanjaro waterfall hike was beautiful start. Each park offered something different - Tarangire for elephants, Serengeti for vast landscapes and predators, Ngorongoro for concentrated wildlife. Camping brought us close to nature - falling asleep to animal sounds was magical. Cultural visits with local tribes were respectful and educational, not tourist circus. Guide was excellent storyteller, sharing both wildlife facts and local history. Group size was perfect at six people. Food cooked by camp staff was surprisingly good. This great option for adventurous travelers wanting authentic experience beyond luxury lodges. Felt like real African adventure!',
