  excerpt: 'Maasai village experience felt genuine. Boat safari peaceful and productive.',
  fullReview: 'What distinguished this safari was meaningful cultural component. Maasai village visit felt authentic - stayed several hours, learned about traditional medicine, watched beadwork, shared meal, heard stories about lion hunting traditions. Not rushed tourist stop but real cultural exchange. Wildlife aspects were strong too - boat safari on Rufiji River offered unique perspective seeing hippos and crocodiles from water level. Mikumi delivered good game drives with elephant herds and predators. Nyerere walking safari was thrilling. Accommodations simple but adequate. Guide balanced wildlife expertise with cultural sensitivity. For travelers wanting safari plus genuine cultural understanding, this excellent choice. Felt like experienced Tanzania, not just photographed animals.',
