date: 'February 5, 2024',
excerpt: 'Wild dogs! Remote location. Felt like real unexplored Africa.',
fullReview: `Ruaha was absolutely spectacular and criminally underrated! So remote we often didn't see another vehicle entire day. Wildlife was phenomenal - saw endangered wild dogs hunting (guide said extremely rare sighting!), massive lion prides, huge elephant herds, kudu, roan antelope. Landscapes were dramatic and varied - baobab forests, river valleys, rocky escarpments. SGR train from Dar was comfortable scenic journey. Mikumi warm-up day was productive. Ruaha camps were authentic bush experience - basic but comfortable, great food, fell asleep to roaring lions. Guide was passionate about park and knew it intimately. This for serious wildlife enthusiasts wanting authentic remote experience away from tourist crowds. Absolutely incredible!`,
