date: 'May 26, 2023',
excerpt: 'First safari ever and this was perfect! Great value, saw so much.',
fullReview: `As first-time safari goers, this was perfect introduction! Three days covered highlights without overwhelming us. Tarangire elephants were incredible - babies playing while mothers watched protectively. Ngorongoro Crater was mind-blowing with all Big Five in single location - lions, rhinos, buffalo, elephants, leopard all spotted! Lake Manyara had beautiful landscapes and flamingos. Camping was adventure itself - sleeping in tents hearing animal sounds was magical. Group dynamics were fun - six travelers from different countries sharing experiences. Guide was patient with our endless questions and newbie mistakes. Food surprisingly good. This excellent entry-level safari that doesn't compromise on wildlife. Already planning longer, more expensive return trip!`,
