date: 'October 8, 2024',
excerpt: 'Walking safari exhilarating! Felt dangerous and real. Incredible experience.',
fullReview: 'Walking safari in Ruaha was most exhilarating experience of my life! Armed guide led us tracking lion pride - adrenaline pumping as we followed fresh tracks through bush. Came dangerously close to buffalo (they can be aggressive) before carefully retreating. Every sound, smell, footprint mattered. Learned about plants, insects, bird calls, dung identification. Felt like part of ecosystem rather than tourist observer. Regular game drives excellent too - saw wild dogs, massive elephant herds, lions. Great Ruaha River scenery beautiful. Camp rustic authentic with amazing night sounds. This not for everyone - requires physical fitness, courage, and adventure spirit. But for those wanting deeper wilder connection with African bush, absolutely transformative experience!',
