date: 'July 23, 2022',
excerpt: `River crossing was most dramatic thing I've witnessed! Unbelievable!`,
fullReview: 'Words cannot adequately describe witnessing Great Migration! Spent entire day at Mara River watching thousands upon thousands of wildebeest gathering, hesitating, finally plunging into water en masse. Crocodiles attacking, wildebeest panicking, sheer chaos and drama everywhere! Saw at least five kills. Heard thundering hooves, bellowing animals, splashing water. Most intense dramatic natural spectacle imaginable! Days following migration across plains - endless columns stretching horizon to horizon. Dust clouds, constant movement, predators circling. Ngorongoro and Tarangire were excellent additions. Lodges beautiful. Guide expert at predicting migration movement. This once-in-lifetime bucket list experience. Worth every penny. Cannot recommend strongly enough!',
