sceneryRating: 4.9,
birdingRating: 5.0,
date: 'November 14, 2024',
excerpt: 'Incredible bird diversity! Guide knew every species. Perfect for birders.',
fullReview: 'As dedicated bird photographer, this tour was absolute paradise! Guide was serious experienced birder himself - knew calls instantly, predicted behaviors, positioned vehicle perfectly for photography. Lake Manyara incredible diversity - thousands of flamingos, pelicans, various storks, fish eagles, countless waterbirds. Tarangire provided raptors, rollers, endemic species. Ngorongoro massive flamingo flocks on soda lake plus highland specialties. Documented over 260 species in three days! Mammals were wonderful bonus - elephants, Big Five - but birds were real treasure. Guide extremely patient with our photography requirements - waiting for perfect light, ideal angles. Lodges comfortable with early breakfast accommodating dawn birding. Specialized tour perfect for serious birders and photographers. Cannot recommend enough!',
