sceneryRating: 4.7,
birdingRating: 4.5,
date: 'July 27, 2024',
excerpt: 'Wild dogs hunting! Massive lion prides. True wilderness. Spectacular!',
fullReview: 'Ruaha absolutely exceeded expectations - criminally underrated! Remote location meant often entire hours without seeing another vehicle. Wildlife phenomenal - witnessed endangered wild dogs coordinating hunt (guide said incredibly rare privilege!), encountered massive lion prides 20+ individuals, huge elephant herds, beautiful kudu and sable antelope. Landscapes dramatically varied - ancient baobab forests, riverside woodlands, rocky granite outcrops. SGR train journey from Dar comfortable and scenic. Mikumi provided excellent warm-up day. Ruaha camps authentic bush experience - rustic yet comfortable, excellent food, fell asleep to nearby lion roars! Guide deeply passionate about park with intimate knowledge. Perfect for serious wildlife enthusiasts wanting authentic remote wilderness away from northern circuit crowds. Absolutely spectacular experience!',
helpful: 401,
verified: true,
tourTaken: '4-Day Astonish Mikumi NP and Ruaha National Park',
tourId: '4-day-astonish-mikumi-ruaha-national-park'
