date: 'December 2, 2024',
excerpt: 'First safari - perfect! Incredible wildlife, great price. Already planning return!',
fullReview: 'As first-time safari travelers, this was absolutely perfect introduction! Three days efficiently covered Tanzania highlights. Tarangire elephants were magnificent - watched babies playing, mothers protectively hovering. Ngorongoro Crater mind-blowing - all Big Five in single stunning location! Lions, rhinos, buffalo, elephants, even distant leopard! Lake Manyara provided beautiful landscapes and pink flamingo carpets. Camping added authenticity - falling asleep hearing mysterious animal sounds was magical experience! Group small and friendly - six travelers bonding over shared excitement. Guide patiently answered countless beginner questions. Food surprisingly tasty. Excellent entry-level safari maintaining high wildlife standards despite budget price. Already planning longer return trip after this amazing introduction! Highly recommend for first-timers!',
