  sceneryRating: 4.5,
  birdingRating: 3.5,
  date: 'January 18, 2025',
  excerpt: `Sunrise beautiful but flight too short and expensive. Mixed feelings overall.`,
  fullReview: `Hot air balloon ride was undeniably scenic - sunrise over Serengeti stunning, aerial perspective unique. However, actual flight lasted only 40 minutes for $580 per person which felt extremely overpriced. Champagne breakfast nice but didn't justify cost. Regular game drives were adequate though never found big predator action we hoped for - mostly zebras, wildebeest, distant elephants. Guide seemed distracted, took phone calls during drives which was annoying. Fly-in convenience appreciated but lodges weren't as luxurious as website photos suggested - rooms smaller, pool needed maintenance. Food mediocre. While had some good moments, overall felt prices inflated without proportional quality. Standard driving safari probably better value. Expected more for premium pricing.`,
