  countryFlag: 'dk',
  title: 'Best budget safari value',
  rating: 4.6,
  wildlifeRating: 4.7,
  bushVibe: 4.4,
  sceneryRating: 4.8,
  birdingRating: 4.5,
  date: 'February 18, 2025',
  excerpt: `First-time safari perfect! Incredible wildlife at budget price! Loved it!`,
  fullReview: `As first-time safari travelers, this was absolutely ideal introduction! Three days efficiently covered Tanzania's greatest highlights. Tarangire elephants were magnificent - watched adorable babies playing while protective mothers hovered nearby. Ngorongoro Crater absolutely mind-blowing - all Big Five in single stunning location! Spotted lions, rare black rhinos, buffalo, elephants, even distant leopard! Lake Manyara provided beautiful landscapes and pink flamingo carpets. Camping added wonderful authenticity - falling asleep to mysterious animal sounds was magical memorable experience! Group small and friendly - seven travelers from different countries bonding over shared excitement. Guide patiently answered countless beginner questions. Food surprisingly tasty. Excellent entry-level safari maintaining high wildlife standards despite budget pricing. Already planning longer return trip!`,
  helpful: 389,
  verified: true,
