migration: {
    title: 'The Great Wildebeest Migration',
    description: 'Tanzania hosts the world\'s most spectacular wildlife phenomenon - the Great Wildebeest Migration. Over 1.5 million wildebeest, 200,000 zebras, and countless gazelles traverse the iconic Serengeti plains in an endless cycle of life. Witness dramatic river crossings at the Grumeti and Mara Rivers from June to July, calving season from January to March, and year-round predator action. This UNESCO World Heritage spectacle offers unparalleled safari experiences that define African wildlife adventure.'
  },

  highlights: {
    title: 'Premier Wildlife Safari Experiences',
    description: 'Tanzania delivers Africa\'s most extraordinary wildlife encounters across its world-renowned national parks. Experience the Big Five in the wildlife-rich Ngorongoro Crater, witness massive elephant herds in Tarangire National Park, and track lions and leopards across the endless Serengeti plains. Marvel at chimpanzees in Gombe and Mahale, spot rare wild dogs in Ruaha, and observe hippo pods in Katavi. From Mount Kilimanjaro\'s majestic backdrop to the pristine beaches of Zanzibar, Tanzania combines authentic safari adventures with diverse ecosystems that create unforgettable African wildlife photography opportunities and bucket-list safari moments.'
  },

  bestTime: {
    title: 'Best Time to Visit Tanzania for Safari',
    description: 'Tanzania offers exceptional year-round safari experiences, with June to October ranking as the optimal Dry season for wildlife viewing. The Great Migration\'s dramatic river crossings occur from June to July in the Western Corridor, while the northern Serengeti witnesses the spectacle from July to October. January to March is prime time for wildebeest calving season in the southern Serengeti, offering incredible predator interactions. The Dry season (June-October) provides excellent game viewing across Ngorongoro Crater, Tarangire, and Ruaha National Parks, with concentrated wildlife around water sources. November to May brings lush landscapes, exceptional bird watching with migratory species, and fewer crowds for budget-conscious travelers seeking authentic Tanzania safari adventures.'
  },

