wildlifePreview: {
        description: `Uganda is Africa's ultimate primate safari destination, home to nearly half of the world's remaining mountain gorillas in Bwindi Impenetrable Forest. Track endangered chimpanzees in Kibale Forest, spot tree-climbing lions in Queen Elizabeth National Park, and witness the Big Five across diverse ecosystems. Murchison Falls offers thrilling Nile boat safaris with hippos, crocodiles, and massive elephant herds, while the remote Kidepo Valley delivers untouched wilderness encounters. From gorilla trekking permits to birdwatching paradise (1,000+ species), Uganda combines affordable safari experiences with authentic wildlife encounters that create memories of a lifetime.`,
        linkText: 'More about the wildlife'
      },

      thingsToDoPreview: [
        {
          description: `Uganda offers unforgettable adventure activities beyond its world-famous gorilla trekking. Experience white-water rafting at the Source of the Nile in Jinja, trek the legendary Rwenzori Mountains (Mountains of the Moon), or track golden monkeys in Mgahinga National Park. Explore scenic crater lakes, hike through rainforest canopies, and take boat safaris on the Kazinga Channel teeming with wildlife. Immerse yourself in authentic cultural tours with local communities, then discover Uganda's vibrant city life in Kampala. From primate tracking to adventure sports, Uganda delivers diverse experiences for every type of traveler.`,
          linkText: "Activities to do"       
        },
      ],

      weatherPreview: {
        description: `Uganda's equatorial climate offers year-round safari opportunities with warm, pleasant temperatures perfect for gorilla trekking and wildlife viewing. The country experiences two dry seasons (December to February and June to September)—ideal times for mountain gorilla permits, chimpanzee tracking, and game drives with excellent wildlife visibility. Uganda's tropical weather ensures lush, green landscapes even during drier months, while the wet seasons bring spectacular birdwatching opportunities and fewer crowds. With its moderate highland climate and consistent temperatures, Uganda provides comfortable safari conditions throughout the year, making it a flexible destination for planning your East African adventure.`,
        linkText: 'More about the weather and climate'
      },

      bestTimePreview: {
        description: `Uganda is an exceptional year-round safari destination, with peak seasons offering optimal conditions for gorilla trekking and wildlife viewing. The dry seasons (June to September and December to February) provide the best gorilla trekking experience with easier forest trails, excellent primate tracking conditions, and prime game viewing in Queen Elizabeth and Murchison Falls National Parks. The wet seasons (March to May and October to November) offer lower gorilla permit prices, fewer tourists, and incredible birdwatching opportunities with migratory species. Whether you're seeking mountain gorilla encounters, chimpanzee tracking, or Big Five safaris, Uganda's diverse ecosystems and affordable safari packages make it the perfect East African destination any time of year.`,
        linkText: 'More about the best time to visit'
      },

