  date: 'September 23, 2025',
  excerpt: 'Four days of profound mountain gorilla experiences followed by productive wildlife drives.',
  fullReview: 'Our gorilla trekking experience was profoundly emotional and exceeded all expectations despite significant physical challenge. Bwindi Impenetrable Forest definitely lives up to its name - the trek was strenuous through dense undergrowth, steep muddy slopes, and thick vegetation. Finding our assigned gorilla family felt like discovering precious treasure after difficult journey. We observed intimate family interactions including mutual grooming sessions, juveniles playing chase games in trees, mothers nursing tiny infants, and silverback\'s impressive protective presence. The allocated hour passed far too quickly during this privileged wildlife encounter. Queen Elizabeth National Park provided excellent contrast with open savannah landscapes and different species. Game drives produced large elephant families with babies, massive buffalo herds, various antelope species, and distant lions. Kazinga Channel boat safari was highlight for aquatic wildlife photography with abundant hippos displaying aggressive territorial behavior, crocodiles sunbathing, and spectacular bird diversity. Mid-range accommodations offered good comfort after long trekking days. Guide was knowledgeable about gorilla behavior and conservation challenges. Worthwhile investment.',
