  excerpt: 'Four days offering authentic mountain gorilla encounters and Queen Elizabeth wildlife at fair prices.',
  fullReview: 'This mid-range safari package provided excellent gorilla trekking experience at reasonable pricing without luxury overhead costs. Gorilla permits represent the major expense regardless of accommodation level chosen. Bwindi forest trek was physically challenging through steep terrain and dense vegetation, but finding our gorilla family after 4-hour hike made every difficult step absolutely worthwhile. We observed natural gorilla behaviors including feeding on bamboo shoots, juveniles playing wrestling games, mothers grooming infants protectively, and massive silverback watching over family group. The privileged hour passed too quickly during this unforgettable wildlife encounter. Queen Elizabeth National Park game drives yielded good wildlife variety with elephants, large buffalo herds, Uganda kob with distinctive horns, warthogs, and various antelope species. Kazinga Channel boat cruise highlighted aquatic wildlife with abundant hippos displaying territorial aggression, crocodiles sunbathing on banks, and good birding opportunities. Accommodations were comfortable mid-range lodges with friendly staff and decent meals. Nothing luxurious but perfectly adequate after long trekking days. Guide was professional and knowledgeable. Perfect choice for budget-conscious gorilla enthusiasts.',
