 bestTimeToGoByMajorPark: `The best time to visit Uganda depends on your wildlife and safari interests. The Dry Seasons June to September and December to February are ideal for gorilla trekking in Bwindi Impenetrable Forest, chimpanzee tracking in Kibale, and game viewing in Queen Elizabeth and Murchison Falls National Parks, as thinning vegetation and lower water levels make animals easier to spot. The Wet Seasons (March to May and October to November) are perfect for birdwatching safaris, with lush green forests, active primates, and the arrival of migratory and endemic birds across Uganda’s wetlands, crater lakes, and savannas, providing a premium wildlife safari and birding experience.`,


