  malariaRisk: {
    title: 'Malaria Risk',
    description: 'Malaria is present in most parts of Uganda, particularly in lowland regions, lake basins, river valleys, and many national parks, including areas around Lake Victoria, Murchison Falls, Queen Elizabeth, and Kidepo Valley. Higher-altitude regions above approximately 1,800–2,000 meters, such as parts of the southwestern highlands near Bwindi Impenetrable Forest and the Rwenzori Mountains, generally have a lower risk, though malaria can still occur. Transmission is highest during and immediately after the rainy seasons (March–May and September–November). Travelers are strongly advised to consult a healthcare professional before travel for appropriate malaria prevention measures, including prophylactic medication, insect repellent, and protective clothing.'
  },

