wildlifePreview: {
  description: `Rwanda is a premier primate safari destination, protecting endangered mountain gorillas in the accessible Volcanoes National Park with some of the world's most intimate wildlife encounters. Track chimpanzees through ancient Nyungwe Forest, spot golden monkeys in the Virunga Mountains, and experience complete Big Five safaris in the successfully restored Akagera National Park. From gorilla trekking permits to canopy walks above pristine rainforest, Rwanda combines world-class conservation with luxury safari experiences. This compact nation delivers Africa's most inspiring wildlife recovery story, where lions and rhinos have been reintroduced and gorilla populations continue to thrive under exceptional protection.`,
  linkText: 'More about the wildlife'
},

thingsToDoPreview: [
  {
    description: `Rwanda offers extraordinary experiences beyond its legendary gorilla trekking adventures. Walk among the clouds on Nyungwe's thrilling canopy walkway suspended above ancient rainforest, explore the scenic beauty of Lake Kivu with kayaking and island hopping, or track golden monkeys through bamboo forests. Discover Rwanda's remarkable history at the Kigali Genocide Memorial, hike to Dian Fossey's gravesite in the Virungas, and engage with local communities through cultural village tours. From luxury safari lodges to vibrant Kigali city experiences, Rwanda seamlessly blends wildlife conservation, adventure activities, and cultural immersion into unforgettable journeys.`,
    linkText: "Activities to do"       
  },
],

weatherPreview: {
  description: `Rwanda's temperate highland climate provides comfortable year-round safari conditions with mild temperatures ideal for gorilla trekking and wildlife activities. The country experiences two dry seasons (June to September and December to February)—perfect for mountain gorilla permits, easier trekking conditions, and excellent game viewing in Akagera National Park. Rwanda's "eternal spring" climate keeps landscapes beautifully green throughout the year, while the wet seasons offer lush forest conditions and outstanding primate photography opportunities. With its moderate mountain temperatures and consistent weather patterns, Rwanda ensures pleasant trekking experiences any time of year, making safari planning flexible for this compact East African gem.`,
  linkText: 'More about the weather and climate'
},

bestTimePreview: {
  description: `Rwanda is an excellent year-round safari destination, with dry seasons offering optimal conditions for gorilla trekking and Big Five safaris. The peak dry seasons (June to September and December to February) provide the best gorilla trekking experience with drier mountain trails, comfortable hiking conditions, and prime wildlife viewing in Akagera National Park. The wet seasons (March to May and October to November) bring quieter parks, lush forest scenery, and exceptional primate photography with dramatic cloud-covered volcanic landscapes. Whether you're planning mountain gorilla encounters, chimpanzee tracking in Nyungwe, or combining multiple parks, Rwanda's compact size and world-class conservation make it Africa's most efficient and rewarding primate safari destination throughout the year.`,
  linkText: 'More about the best time to visit'
},

