  fullReview: `Rwanda represents the gold standard in primate tourism. Volcanoes National Park offers the most accessible and well-managed gorilla trekking in Africa, with strict conservation protocols ensuring both animal welfare and visitor safety. The addition of golden monkey tracking provides a dynamic contrast—these playful, endangered primates offer a lighter, more energetic encounter. What sets Rwanda apart is its commitment to sustainable tourism: permit fees directly fund conservation and community development, while luxury lodges operate with minimal environmental impact. The infrastructure is excellent, the guides are among the continent's best trained, and the experience feels both exclusive and purposeful. For travelers who want a focused, high-impact primate safari in a compact timeframe, this is the premier choice.`,
