migration: {
  title: 'World-Class Gorilla Trekking Experiences',
  description: `Rwanda is globally renowned as the premier destination for mountain gorilla encounters, offering travelers transformative wildlife experiences in the stunning Volcanoes National Park. Trek through bamboo forests and volcanic slopes to meet endangered mountain gorillas in their natural habitat, track playful golden monkeys through misty highlands, and discover chimpanzees in the ancient Nyungwe Forest. These expertly guided, sustainable primate experiences showcase Rwanda's commitment to conservation and deliver intimate, emotional connections with some of the world's rarest and most endangered species, making it an essential bucket-list safari destination.`
},

highlights: {
  title: 'Exceptional Wildlife & Safari Adventures',
  description: `Rwanda combines iconic primate encounters with diverse safari experiences across its beautifully managed national parks. Track endangered mountain gorillas and golden monkeys in Volcanoes National Park, enjoy Big Five game drives in Akagera National Park featuring lions, elephants, black rhinos, leopards, and buffalo, and trek for chimpanzees in Nyungwe Forest, one of Africa's oldest and most biodiverse rainforests. Experience boat safaris on Lake Ihema past hippos and crocodiles, discover over 700 bird species including rare Albertine Rift endemics, and explore the stunning landscapes of rolling hills, volcanic peaks, and pristine wilderness. With excellent infrastructure, luxury eco-lodges, exceptional guiding standards, and uncrowded parks, Rwanda delivers seamless, high-end safari experiences perfect for discerning travelers, wildlife photographers, and conservation-minded adventurers.`
},

bestTime: {
  title: 'Best Time to Visit Rwanda for Safari',
  description: `Rwanda offers excellent year-round safari conditions, with the best gorilla trekking and wildlife viewing occurring during the Dry seasons from June to September and December to February. These months provide easier hiking conditions in Volcanoes National Park, optimal chimpanzee tracking in Nyungwe Forest, and prime game viewing in Akagera National Park as animals congregate around water sources. The Wet seasons from March to May and October to November bring lush green landscapes, incredible birdwatching opportunities with migratory species, vibrant photography conditions, and fewer tourists along with more competitive lodge pricing. Thanks to Rwanda's temperate climate, high altitude, and well-maintained park infrastructure, travelers can enjoy exceptional gorilla encounters and wildlife safaris throughout the year.`
},
