 bestTimeToGoByMajorPark: `The best time to visit Rwanda depends on your wildlife and safari interests. The Dry Seasons, from June to September and December to February, are ideal for gorilla trekking in Volcanoes National Park, chimpanzee tracking in Nyungwe Forest, and game viewing in Akagera National Park, as thinning vegetation and lower water levels make animals easier to spot. The Wet Seasons (April to May and November) are perfect for birdwatching safaris, with lush green forests, active primates, and the arrival of migratory and Albertine Rift near-endemic birds across Rwanda’s forests, wetlands, and savannas, providing a premium wildlife and birding experience.`,


