malariaRisk: {
  title: 'Malaria Risk',
  description: 'Malaria is present throughout most parts of Rwanda, especially in lowland regions, wetlands, and areas near lakes and rivers, including Akagera National Park and the southern and western lowlands. Higher-altitude regions such as the Volcanoes National Park and Nyungwe Forest generally have lower risk, though malaria can still occur. Transmission peaks during and just after the rainy seasons (March–May and October–November). Travelers are strongly advised to consult a healthcare professional before travel for appropriate malaria prevention, including prophylactic medication, insect repellent, and protective clothing.'
},

