migration: {
  title: 'Epic Big Five Safari Experiences',
  description: `South Africa is renowned for world-class Big Five safaris, offering travelers unforgettable wildlife encounters across iconic parks and private game reserves. Embark on expertly guided game drives in Kruger National Park, Addo Elephant, and Hluhluwe-iMfolozi to spot lions, elephants, rhinos, leopards, and buffalo, or explore exclusive private reserves like Sabi Sands and Phinda for intimate, crowd-free experiences. Beyond the bush, discover marine wildlife with whale watching in Hermanus, shark cage diving in Gansbaai, and penguin encounters at Boulders Beach. With luxury lodges, conservation-focused experiences, and breathtaking landscapes ranging from savannah plains to dramatic coastlines, South Africa delivers transformative safari adventures for wildlife enthusiasts, photographers, and discerning travelers alike.`
},

highlights: {
  title: 'Diverse Wildlife & Unforgettable Safaris',
  description: `South Africa offers a remarkable range of wildlife and safari adventures. Witness the Big Five on guided game drives across Kruger, Madikwe, and private reserves like Kapama and Thornybush, track rare predators in Kgalagadi Transfrontier Park, or spot elephants in Addo Elephant National Park. Birdwatching enthusiasts can discover hundreds of species, while coastal safaris provide whale migrations, penguin colonies, and shark encounters. Explore the stunning landscapes of the Garden Route, Drakensberg Mountains, and Cape Winelands, combining thrilling wildlife with dramatic scenery and cultural experiences. With top-tier lodges, expert guides, and well-managed parks, South Africa ensures seamless, high-end safari journeys for all adventurers.`
},

bestTime: {
  title: 'Best Time to Visit South Africa for Safari',
  description: `South Africa offers excellent safari opportunities year-round, with the dry winter months from May to September providing optimal conditions for Big Five sightings as animals gather around waterholes. Game drives are more rewarding, bush visibility is higher, and malaria risk is lower in northern parks like Kruger. The wet summer season from October to April brings lush green landscapes, newborn wildlife, and spectacular birdwatching, while coastal regions offer whale watching from June to November. With diverse climates across national parks, private reserves, and marine destinations, travelers can enjoy exceptional wildlife, unforgettable scenery, and immersive safari experiences throughout the year.`
},
