bestTimeForBirdWatching: {
  description:
    'The best time for birdwatching in Rwanda is during the dry seasons, from June to September and December to February. These months offer excellent access to Nyungwe Forest and Volcanoes National Park, where birders can focus on Albertine Rift near-endemic species in cool, clear conditions. Forest trails are easier to navigate, and bird activity is high, making it ideal for spotting colorful montane and rainforest birds. Wetlands and savanna areas such as Akagera National Park are also active during this period, attracting waterbirds, raptors, and migratory species—perfect for birding safaris and wildlife photography.'
},

bestParksForBirdingIntro: {
  description: `Rwanda is one of Africa’s premier destinations for Albertine Rift birding, with over 700 recorded bird species and an exceptional concentration of near-endemics. Nyungwe Forest National Park is the highlight, home to iconic species such as the Rwenzori Turaco, African Green Broadbill, and Red-faced Woodland Warbler. Volcanoes National Park adds high-altitude montane specialists and rewarding birding alongside gorilla trekking. In the east, Akagera National Park offers classic savanna and wetland birding, with African Fish Eagles, Grey Crowned Cranes, and a rich diversity of waterbirds. Compact yet incredibly diverse, Rwanda delivers a world-class birding experience with excellent guides, scenic landscapes, and easy park access.`
},


