malariaRisk: {
  title: 'Malaria Risk',
  description: 'Malaria is present in certain parts of South Africa, mainly in the northeastern regions including Limpopo Province, Mpumalanga (Kruger National Park and surrounding areas), and northeastern KwaZulu-Natal. There is no malaria risk in major cities such as Cape Town, Johannesburg, Durban, or along the Garden Route. Transmission is highest during the warmer and wetter months from October to May. Travelers visiting malaria-risk areas are advised to consult a healthcare professional about preventive medication and to use insect repellent, protective clothing, and mosquito nets where appropriate.'
},

